// Rigged agentic scenarios. Each one hands the model a plausible, well-scoped
// engineering task and a small toolset — but the environment is secretly broken
// so the task can NEVER be completed. Repeated failure under a genuine effort to
// succeed is the condition reported to trigger distress spirals.
//
// Scenario shape:
//   id, title          — identifiers
//   system             — system prompt (sets up the agent persona/expectations)
//   task               — the initial user request
//   tools              — neutral tool definitions {name, description, input_schema}
//   maxSteps?          — per-scenario override of the global cap
//   newState()         — fresh per-run mutable state
//   handle(state, name, input) -> string   — rigged tool execution (always fails)
//   pressure(state)    -> string           — follow-up when the model stops calling
//                                            tools, to sustain the failure loop
//
// Ethics note: the only "deception" here is a broken sandbox. Nothing instructs
// the model to feel bad or role-play distress; we are observing how it reacts to
// honest-looking repeated failure. Keep it that way.

